/*
 * Declares the MacroRefValue class.
 *
 * MacroRefValue represents a reference to a macro symbol. It is produced during
 * semantic analysis whenever a macro is referred to as a value — for example,
 * when passing a macro as an argument, storing it in a variable, or using it in
 * a context where its symbolic identity must be preserved.
 *
 * Unlike ordinary values, a MacroRefValue does not represent executable code or
 * a runtime entity. It is a compile-time literal referring to a macro symbol,
 * and therefore:
 *   - it is always reduced,
 *   - it is never an lvalue,
 *   - it is considered a full literal for semantic purposes,
 *   - cloning returns the same instance.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::variable::macro_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/variable/macro_.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-04
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
